Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:04:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: an HDR film does not set the 3D output a second time

Kodi learns a film's HDR type from its first configured picture, which
can come a moment after the stereo mode has entered HFR VRR. The HDR
type change then forced a mode switch of its own: 1080p165 was set a
second time 0.3 s after the first (seen on 2 of 4 HDR10 and Dolby Vision
3D starts), losing the picture again and resetting the TV, the eARC
link and the receiver once more.

In HFR VRR the output's format does not depend on HDR10 or HLG: the
kernel signals them from each frame on the mode already set. So there an
HDR type change between none, HDR10, HLG and HDR10+ keeps the window
and only records the new type. A change to or from Dolby Vision still
sets the mode: the link format is the DV tunnel's.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
@@ -183,6 +183,10 @@
   // the output's 120/119.88 Hz follows the film there, not Kodi's resolution
   if (fs3d_same)
     force_mode_switch_by_fractional_rate = false;
+  // there the kernel signals HDR10 and HLG frame by frame; Dolby Vision sets the link
+  if (fs3d_same && hdrType != StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION &&
+      m_hdrType != StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION)
+    force_mode_switch_by_hdr = false;
 
   // check if mode switch is needed
   if ((fs3d_same ||
@@ -197,6 +201,7 @@
       !force_mode_switch_by_stereo_mode && !force_mode_switch_by_fs3d_rate)
   {
     CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "CWinSystemAmlogicGLESContext::{}: No need to create a new window", __FUNCTION__);
+    m_hdrType = hdrType;
     // the surface stays as it is, stacked HFR VRR GUI included
     int eyeWidth = 0;
     int eyeHeight = 0;
